  "note": "Election of the Cookstown Urban District Council, ordinary day 15 January 1925; the retiring members were re-elected with one new member, no contest (Northern Whig, 10 January 1925, p. 10). 'The retiring members of Cookstown Urban Council, Messrs. J. D. Anderson, William M'Clay and W. H. Newell, have been re-elected, with Mr. Thomas E. Elmes.' The report records no contest; no party label is printed. Returned unopposed."
